\section{Visual replication by training seed}\label{app:seeds}
The three systems share demonstrations, pretrained initialization, architecture and development environment/clock arrangements. New systems generate their own native development labels. These results test training randomness under those fixed conditions, not new demonstration collections, new pretraining or task-distribution shift. No weak source, seed or task is excluded. Native success labels in the older replication are retained rollout outputs; its archived reward/action arrays do not independently reconstruct a complete success-flag history. The newer visual channel experiment stores the full flags. Original historical source-budget controls and all detailed study contrasts are in Online Resource 1.

